      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A patient with coronary disease class III of the New York Heart Association and tracheal stenosis with a tracheo-oesophageal fistula, which developed after long-term intubation, is described. As both conditions were symptomatic, an aortocoronary double bypass was combined with resection of the trachea and closure of the fistula. Postoperative recovery was uneventful and the patient is symptom-free after 3 years."},
